From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): decode Bedrock dimension height ranges

Protocol 2193 encodes DIMENSION_DATA bounds as minimum Y followed by a
height range, rather than the earlier maximum/minimum pair. Compute the
exclusive upper bound as minimum plus range before storing the existing
min/max dimension definition. Preserve negative minima, reject nonpositive
ranges, and detect overflow instead of creating an invalid Java height.

Mojang's 1.26.50-preview.26 metadata (protocol 2192) identifies Minimum Y
at ordinal 0 and Height Range at ordinal 1. The 1.26.51 metadata (2193)
retains those fields. Cloudburst's target-specific 2193 serializer reads
minimum first and adds the second field to obtain maximum; its 2168
serializer still uses the old maximum/minimum representation:
https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/releases/tag/v1.26.50-preview.26
https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/releases/tag/v1.26.51
https://github.com/CloudburstMC/Protocol/blob/3.0/bedrock-codec/src/main/java/org/cloudburstmc/protocol/bedrock/codec/v2193/serializer/DimensionDataSerializer_v2193.java

An official Bedrock 1.26.51.1 Hive capture confirms a minecraft:overworld
entry with minimum 0 and range 256 before StartGame. Native spawning
succeeds, while treating those fields as maximum/minimum exports height
-256 and prevents ViaBedrock's chunk tracker from initializing. No packet
or server asset from that private capture is included here.

Synthetic packet tests cover zero, negative and positive minimum heights,
remaining-field alignment, signed bounds, nonpositive ranges and overflow.
Configuration-only overworld handling remains as before.

Validation: Java 17 full core suite passes 265 tests across 75 suites, with 0 skipped; main and test Checkstyle pass.

Retain the protocol-2225 cloud height and visibility alongside dimension
bounds instead of consuming them without a rendering effect. Project
height through Java 26.3 environment attributes. Suppress disabled clouds
with transparent cloud color, whose zero alpha survives Java's multiplying
day timeline. Keep the other authored dimension attributes intact.

Mojang's 1.26.60 DimensionDefinition schema and developer note us_1665751
establish the new fields. The matching Java 26.3 LevelExtractor and day
timeline establish cloud-height lookup and alpha-based cloud admission.
Cover complete packet boundaries, signed bounds and registry projection.
